\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Judge eternal, throned in splendouur,
\par Lord of lords, and King of kings,
\par With Thy living fire of judgement
\par Purge this realm of bitter things;
\par Solace all its wide dominion
\par With the healing of Thy wings.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Still the weary folk are pining
\par For the hour that brings release;
\par And the city's crowded clangour
\par Cries aloud for sin to cease;
\par And the homesteads and woodlands
\par Plead in silence for their peace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Crown, O God, Thine own endeavour:
\par Cleave our darkness with Thy sword:
\par Feed the faint and hungry heathen
\par With the richness of Thy Word:
\par Cleanse the body of this empire
\par Through the glory of the Lord.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

